---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

const supportEmail = site.supportEmail || site.email;
---
<Prose title="Terms of use" label="Players / Terms" updated="18 October 2026" description={`Terms for using ${site.name} games and website.`}>
  <p>These terms cover all games by {site.name} ("we", "us"), including Kinfold, and this website. By playing our games or using this website, you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use them.</p>

  <h2>Using our games</h2>
  <p>We give you a personal, non-transferable license to play our games for fun. Please don't copy, modify, resell or reverse-engineer them, and don't use cheats, bots or hacks. The app store you downloaded the game from (Apple or Google) has its own terms, and they apply too.</p>

  <h2>Kids and parents</h2>
  <p>Our games are made for everyone, kids included. Each game asks your age when you first open it, so it can set itself up the right way: players under 13 get child-directed ads and can't create an account. Please answer honestly. If you're under the age of adulthood where you live, please play with a parent's or guardian's OK. Parents: purchases and ad settings can be controlled from your device's family or parental settings. Some future games may be made for older players. Each game's store page shows its age rating.</p>

  <h2>Ads</h2>
  <p>Our free games show ads. Ads are shown by our ad partners, and we don't control what's behind them. Please be careful when an ad takes you outside the game. How ads use data is explained in our <a href={url('/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>If a game sells virtual items, such as hints or removing ads, you're buying a license to use them in that game. They have no real-world value and can't be exchanged for money. Purchases are handled by the App Store or Google Play, and refunds follow their rules. If something you paid for doesn't show up, email <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a> and we'll help.</p>

  <h2>Your progress</h2>
  <p>Your progress is saved on your device. Players 13 and over can sign in (with Apple, Google, a Unity player account or email) to back it up online. Please keep your sign-in safe. You're responsible for what happens on your account. We work hard to keep your progress safe, but we can't promise it will never be lost, for example if you delete the game without signing in or a service goes down.</p>
  <p>You can delete your account at any time in the game: <strong>Profile ▸ Delete account</strong>. See <a href={url('/delete-data/')}>Delete your data</a> for other ways.</p>

  <h2>Our stuff</h2>
  <p>Our games, the {site.name} name and logo, characters, art, music and this website belong to {site.name}. You're welcome to share screenshots and videos of your play, including on streams and social media. Please don't use our name or logo in a way that looks like we made or approved something we didn't.</p>

  <h2>Changes and updates</h2>
  <p>We keep improving our games. Updates may add, change or remove features, and we may stop supporting a game one day. If we change these terms, we'll update this page and the date at the top. Playing after a change means you accept the new terms.</p>

  <h2>The fine print</h2>
  <p>Our games and website are provided "as is". We try hard to keep them bug-free and running, but we can't promise they always will be. As far as the law allows, we're not responsible for indirect losses from using them. Nothing in these terms takes away rights you have under the consumer laws where you live.</p>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Arab Republic of Egypt, and the courts of Cairo handle any disputes. Before that, please email us. Most problems are fixed with a quick reply.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>{site.name}, {site.location}. Player support: <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>. Everything else: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</Prose>
